{
    "$schema": "../schema/registry-item.schema.json",
    "name": "saas-ui-react",
    "title": "SaaS UI — React",
    "description": "Copy-in, user-owned React screens for the Lunora SaaS kit: the dashboard stat row, the project list with its create form and search/sort toolbar, the activity feed grouped by day, and the platform admin's organization table. Framework-agnostic view model under lunora/saas-ui/core, thin React views under lunora/saas-ui/react, and token-aligned CSS — no Tailwind, no component library. Edit anything; upgrades are 3-way merged.",
    "docs": "Import the stylesheet once and render the cards from your dashboard route: `import { OverviewStats, ProjectsCard } from './lunora/saas-ui/react'; import './lunora/saas-ui/styles.css';`. Nothing here subscribes — the route owns the query, because the wiring differs per meta-framework. Pass `useQuery(api.saas.overview)` straight into `payload`, `Date.now()` into `now`, and your mutations into `onCreate`/`onArchive`. Requires the `saas` server item (auto-added). For sign-in and organization screens, add the matching `auth-ui-react` item.",
    "requires": ["saas"],
